    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good way to handle the workshop angle. I'm also curious about instances where the attribution is more... strange. We have a few maps where the iconography is very specific and almost cryptic, suggesting the creator might have belonged to a group that intentionally left no typical professional traceable marks. \n\nHow do we categorize entities that seem to exist outside the standard historical record? If we can't find a name or a workshop, but the evidence points to a non-conventional or even \"shadow\" creator, how do we record that in the `dc.creator` or `dc.description` field without being unprofessional or speculative?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
