      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For highly cryptic or intentionally obscured authorship, it is best to document this uncertainty within the metadata notes using `dc.description` or an extended `dc.relation`. Instead of guessing a formal creator, describe the *nature* of the authorship, such as \"Attribution obscured by thematic iconographic choices\" or \"Creator deliberately unrecorded.\" This maintains neutrality by reporting the observation rather than speculating on the creator's identity, preserving archival integrity.",
      "source": "target",
